==Old English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|ang}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*þankijaną}}. Cognate with {{etyl|ofs|-}} {{term|thenka|lang=ofs}} ({{etyl|fy|-}} {{term|tinke|lang=fy}}), {{etyl|osx|-}} {{term|thenkian|lang=osx}} ({{etyl|nds|-}} {{term|denken|lang=nds}}), {{etyl|odt|-}} {{term|thenken|lang=odt}} ({{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|denken|lang=nl}}), {{etyl|goh|-}} {{term|thenken|lang=goh}} ({{etyl|de|-}} {{term|denken|lang=de}}), {{etyl|non|-}} {{term|þekkja|lang=non}} ({{etyl|gmq-osw|-}} {{term|þækkia|lang=gmq-osw}}, {{etyl|is|-}} {{term|þekkja|lang=is}}), {{etyl|got|-}} {{term|𐌸𐌰𐌲𐌺𐌾𐌰𐌽|tr=þagkjan|sc=Goth|lang=got}}. All ultimately from {{etyl|ine-pro|ang}} {{term/t|ine-pro|*tong-||to think}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈθent͡ʃan/|lang=ang}}

===Verb===
{{ang-verb|head=þenċan}}

